1
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,667
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:42,300
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:44,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:45,267
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,033
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:49,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:51,567
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:53,933
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:56,567
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,200
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:01,167
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,667
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,900
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:13,200
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:15,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:22,567
<i>Victor tried to kill me!
My life is in danger.</i>

21
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:25,733
<i>If you want to survive,
you need to work with us.</i>

22
00:01:25,867 --> 00:01:27,967
<i> That Delgado's so arrogant.</i>

23
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:31,300
<i>Dig into Director Delgado's
records.</i>

24
00:01:31,433 --> 00:01:34,133
<i>I'm sure we can find something
we can use against him.</i>

25
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:36,200
<i>I'm asking for something
so simple.</i>

26
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:39,167
<i>Get over here
before I make you regret it!</i>

27
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,867
<i>Come with us.
You explain it to Umali.</i>

28
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:42,967
<i> Just a reminder, okay?</i>

29
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,667
<i> We came here to have fun.</i>

30
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,133
<i>Let's forget everything
that happened.</i>

31
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:48,133
<i>All the food I'm feeding you
is delicious!</i>

32
00:01:48,267 --> 00:01:50,700
<i>And I'll make sure
you're drowning in booze.</i>

33
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:54,200
<i>We caught Mr. Chan, but
we're the ones taking the fall.</i>

34
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:57,433
<i>Ma'am Pia's furious at you,
and Delgado's mad at us.</i>

35
00:01:57,567 --> 00:01:59,900
<i>I'll head to the bar
so we can order.</i>

36
00:02:00,033 --> 00:02:02,067
<i>- Thank you.
- You shouldn't have.</i>

37
00:02:08,033 --> 00:02:09,867
[DOOR OPENS]

38
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,533
[DOOR CLOSES]

39
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:16,400
[SNIFFLES]

40
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,300
Ma'am.

41
00:02:19,433 --> 00:02:21,933
[SNIFFLES, EXHALES SOFTLY]

42
00:02:22,067 --> 00:02:23,300
Oh...

43
00:02:25,867 --> 00:02:28,467
Are you still mad
about Salvador?

44
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,900
Sir Umali said
they'd handle it

45
00:02:31,033 --> 00:02:34,733
I just feel bad for my dad.
I feel so sorry for him.

46
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:37,300
He's retired, yet they keep
bothering him.

47
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:39,800
He doesn't talk about it,
but I know him well.

48
00:02:39,933 --> 00:02:44,333
I can feel how deeply
this is affecting him.

49
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:47,700
And freezing development in
Ginintuang Lupa made it worse.

50
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:51,500
I need to do something
to help him out.

51
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:53,433
Ma'am...

52
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:56,000
How are you going to do that,
Ma'am?

53
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:59,867
Salvador keeps throwing
new allegations around.

54
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,233
Then I will solve this problem
myself.

55
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,367
I'm going to make
my dad proud.

56
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:15,633
Handle Mr. Chan's transfer
to the safe house right now.

57
00:03:15,767 --> 00:03:18,867
- Copy, sir.
- Okay.

58
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,933
Sir.

59
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:25,833
Sir, are you really trusting
him with the transfer?

60
00:03:25,967 --> 00:03:29,000
Why, Pia?
Is there an issue?

61
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:32,200
There's no issue,
just like with Jacinto.

62
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:36,533
Sir, why not just give
the job to Tuazon?

63
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:38,067
He's good at his job.

64
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:42,733
He listens to orders
and never acts out like others.

65
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:46,200
I can't assign Team Alpha
to the transfer

66
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:49,367
because they disobeyed me.

67
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,667
Sir, Tuazon wasn't even
one of the troublemakers.

68
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,933
To be fair.

69
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,667
My decision is final.

70
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:03,000
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:11,133
[LIVELY MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:04:24,767 --> 00:04:26,500
What are we going to do?

73
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:28,900
We're dead if they find out.

74
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:30,667
[BARTENDER]
Yeah, I'll bring it over.

75
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:31,767
- One for table number two.
- Got it.

76
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,800
- Uh... boss?
- Yeah.

77
00:04:33,933 --> 00:04:36,067
- Excuse me.
- Boss...

78
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:39,100
- I'd like to order a--
- We'd like to order.

79
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:40,833
- Yeah, and add one of those.
- Uh, boss?

80
00:04:40,967 --> 00:04:43,567
- I'd like to order a--
- Hold on, I'm busy!

81
00:04:44,533 --> 00:04:46,067
- What can I get you?
- Is our order ready yet?

82
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,900
- Yeah, I'll bring it over.
- Alright, thanks.

83
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:49,967
Gabo really is amazing,
isn't he?

84
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,000
Even though people look down
on our neighborhood,

85
00:04:53,133 --> 00:04:56,600
and Miss Betchay constantly
belittles him,

86
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:59,100
they don't know how good
his heart actually is.

87
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:02,167
Imagine, all that gold,
and he just returned it.

88
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:05,600
He's likely the last person
who behaves that way.

89
00:05:05,733 --> 00:05:08,767
I'm not even surprised
about that.

90
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:12,133
He's always been like that
since we were young.

91
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:16,533
They're targeting him here,
but he has a good heart.

92
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:19,900
You guys think
way too highly of Gabo.

93
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,767
Maybe he's just saying that.

94
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:25,367
He probably has a cut
of the gold he got.

95
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,400
- That's true.
- [TOLITS] Right?

96
00:05:26,533 --> 00:05:29,500
Anyone who sees
that much gold

97
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:32,933
will get tempted to steal
a bit to have a better life.

98
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:35,000
Don't just believe Gabo blindly.

99
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:36,833
You're forgetting he's
from Ginintuang Lupa.

100
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:39,633
- We all think alike.
- Hey, hey!

101
00:05:40,167 --> 00:05:42,167
Stop saying that about Gabo.

102
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,900
Just because
we're from the same place

103
00:05:44,033 --> 00:05:45,067
doesn't mean
you know him like that.

104
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,733
You haven't been with
him since we were children.

105
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:49,100
And you three...

106
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:54,533
If you don't trust him,
then leave!

107
00:05:54,667 --> 00:05:56,233
Go back to Django!

108
00:05:56,367 --> 00:05:58,600
We're just thinking rationally.

109
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,467
We all have
different ways of thinking.

110
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:04,900
We're thinking rationally.
It's hard to trust someone.

111
00:06:05,033 --> 00:06:06,567
Just shut up.

112
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,167
[SEBASTIAN] Why did you do it?

113
00:06:09,467 --> 00:06:11,267
What were you thinking, Sam?

114
00:06:11,667 --> 00:06:13,233
You didn't inform us
about your plan.

115
00:06:13,867 --> 00:06:17,267
To me!
I could've helped you!

116
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,167
Look at what happened.

117
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,467
Your service was inconvenienced
because of what you guys did.

118
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,267
I know.

119
00:06:26,767 --> 00:06:29,833
It was just me.
I didn't follow the protocol.

120
00:06:30,367 --> 00:06:33,600
I just really want
to catch Mr. Chan.

121
00:06:33,733 --> 00:06:37,300
Because I knew he'd be
the key to finding more

122
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:39,200
about Zafra's illegal plans.

123
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:40,967
His family has such
a big influence.

124
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,200
[KAREN] What kind of mess
did we get ourselves into?

125
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:44,833
It's so hard to get out of.

126
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:50,167
I'm sorry, team.

127
00:06:50,867 --> 00:06:52,100
I'm really sorry.

128
00:06:53,033 --> 00:06:55,733
[KAREN] Sam,
stop blaming yourself.

129
00:06:55,867 --> 00:06:59,267
We know what we did,
and we did it willingly.

130
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,567
We want to support you here.

131
00:07:01,967 --> 00:07:06,267
If we get suspended or
if we get dismissed from duty,

132
00:07:06,767 --> 00:07:08,400
we will not regret it.

133
00:07:10,067 --> 00:07:12,400
The food is taking too long.
I'll go to the bathroom.

134
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:13,933
[DABOY] I'll go with you!

135
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,600
- [TOLITS] Let's go.
- I'll leave you, guys.

136
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:17,133
- Let's go.
- C'mon.

137
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,733
Do you guys see that?

138
00:07:19,867 --> 00:07:22,633
Those three
have terrible attitudes.

139
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:25,133
Boss, I'd like to place
an order, please.

140
00:07:25,267 --> 00:07:27,300
- [BOTTLE RATTLES]
- Can't you see I'm busy?

141
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:29,467
I don't regret what we did.

142
00:07:30,333 --> 00:07:32,333
We might get hit with a lawsuit,

143
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:34,400
and we could go to jail.

144
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:38,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

145
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,933
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

146
00:07:42,067 --> 00:07:44,133
- It's Sir Delgado.
- [CELLPHONE RINGS]

147
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:45,933
Ah...

148
00:07:48,233 --> 00:07:49,467
- [CELLPHONE RINGS]
- Answer it!

149
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,867
- What will I say?
- Anything!

150
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,633
Maybe he just wants
to ask something.

151
00:07:53,767 --> 00:07:54,733
Gabo?

152
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,033
Have you ordered?
I'm starving.

153
00:07:57,167 --> 00:07:58,933
He might hear
that we're at a bar.

154
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:01,200
- Let's go!
- [GABO] He's ignoring me!

155
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:02,600
[TOLITS] Alright.
I'll use the bathroom first.

156
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:04,667
- Let's go.
- I'll come with you.

157
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:06,600
- [CELLPHONE RINGING]
- No, we'll handle it.

158
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:08,400
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

159
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:16,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:22,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,300
Do you have any idea
what happened?

162
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:27,233
[PAQUITO] A man intervened.

163
00:08:27,367 --> 00:08:29,033
They robbed Salvador.

164
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:31,367
Robbed? Did he get beaten up?

165
00:08:32,633 --> 00:08:35,400
Clearly, that idiot got bolder!

166
00:08:35,533 --> 00:08:38,433
He went to the police
station to file a complaint.

167
00:08:38,567 --> 00:08:43,133
This means all your men
are wanted in our precinct.

168
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:44,867
[DJANGO] Well.

169
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:47,100
Aren't you police officers?

170
00:08:47,233 --> 00:08:48,467
You can handle it.

171
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:54,933
You're so arrogant.
You're way too full of yourself.

172
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:58,167
You're nothing like your father!

173
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,367
Go ahead. Shoot me.

174
00:09:03,033 --> 00:09:04,800
Let's see
how brave you are.

175
00:09:04,933 --> 00:09:11,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:16,700
[PAQUITO] Don't embarrass
yourself, Django.

177
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,467
Drop your guns.

178
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:29,267
Umali.

179
00:09:30,033 --> 00:09:31,233
I'm sorry.

180
00:09:31,867 --> 00:09:33,167
This won't happen again.

181
00:09:33,633 --> 00:09:35,633
We didn't need
to reach this point.

182
00:09:36,767 --> 00:09:37,633
Paquito.

183
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,300
We've been doing business
together for a long time.

184
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:42,433
You know me.

185
00:09:42,867 --> 00:09:44,467
You didn't
do what I asked you...

186
00:09:46,033 --> 00:09:47,233
So I won't pay you.

187
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,233
Let's go.

188
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:57,067
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,000
Whoever did this,

190
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:02,133
better pray
that we don't cross paths

191
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,267
because I'll bury him alive.

192
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:12,933
Hey, boss?
Maybe I can start ordering?

193
00:10:13,067 --> 00:10:15,133
My friends are starving.

194
00:10:15,267 --> 00:10:17,733
Can't you see I'm busy?

195
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,567
We'll just have six beers
and o--

196
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,500
I told you I'm still busy.

197
00:10:21,933 --> 00:10:23,833
I wonder why Sir Delgado
is calling.

198
00:10:23,967 --> 00:10:25,600
[ROBERT] It's probably
about Ma'am Sam.

199
00:10:26,333 --> 00:10:29,367
We're the ones doing
the right thing,

200
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,133
yet we still end up looking
like the bad guys.

201
00:10:31,933 --> 00:10:34,033
Don't worry.
I will take care of all of you.

202
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,633
Especially you, Sam.

203
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:38,500
Are you sure
you got us, Sir Seb?

204
00:10:38,633 --> 00:10:39,933
Absolutely. Sure.

205
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:42,933
- I need to use the restroom.
- Me too.

206
00:10:43,067 --> 00:10:45,233
- Thank you, sir.
- I'll go with you.

207
00:10:45,367 --> 00:10:52,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

208
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:58,833
Hey, boss?

209
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:00,933
Can we get
a follow-up on our order?

210
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,467
- Hey, boss.
- What is it?

211
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:09,933
Stop ignoring me
and take my order!

212
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,300
Do you want me
to hit you in the head?

213
00:11:11,433 --> 00:11:13,067
You're taking other
people's orders but mine!

214
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,567
I'm sorry!

215
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:16,000
Will you finally
take my order?

216
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:17,367
Yes, sir!
What's your order?

217
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,033
Six beers, one cocktail,

218
00:11:20,167 --> 00:11:23,167
one crispy pork knuckle,
barbeque, and sisig.

219
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:25,467
- Got it?
- Yes.

220
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:32,667
Are you okay, Sam?

221
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:40,333
Sam, if you need someone...

222
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,167
[SEBASTIAN] I'm right here.

223
00:11:48,567 --> 00:11:52,167
I'll be here to listen to you.

224
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,867
You know what,

225
00:11:58,633 --> 00:12:00,100
we could be...

226
00:12:06,067 --> 00:12:08,933
I believe in you, Sam.

227
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:15,000
I'm right here for you, Sam.

228
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,833
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:12:19,967 --> 00:12:22,300
I'll cover it.

230
00:12:22,433 --> 00:12:25,300
And you take care of the...
[VOICE TRAILS OFF]

231
00:12:27,233 --> 00:12:28,033
Hurry, I need to pee.

232
00:12:28,033 --> 00:12:29,833
[MAN GAGGING]

233
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:31,400
You keep throwing up, man!

234
00:12:32,433 --> 00:12:34,700
Dude, you smell like
a sapodilla. Pack it up!

235
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:36,833
- You're too drunk, man.
- [ZIPPER ZIPS OPEN]

236
00:12:37,433 --> 00:12:39,133
- It's such a waste, isn't it?
- [DOOR CLOSES]

237
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:42,033
Could a 100,000 pesos hold
a candle to a few gold bars?

238
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:43,267
Do the math for me.

239
00:12:43,267 --> 00:12:45,833
[LAUGHS] If it were me,
it's all mine.

240
00:12:45,833 --> 00:12:47,700
I'd keep those bars
all to myself!

241
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:50,933
But we know Gabo.
He's a thug for real!

242
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:53,033
But he has his own principles.

243
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:55,667
- He'll only do the right thing.
- [PEE SPLASHING]

244
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,267
What did you say?

245
00:12:57,267 --> 00:13:00,067
Principles! You know,
something like, justice!

246
00:13:00,067 --> 00:13:02,867
What's the use of principles
if your stomach is growling?

247
00:13:02,867 --> 00:13:04,800
There was gold just within
his grasp!

248
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:07,067
If it were me, you'll never hear
from me again.

249
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:09,133
- For real? Not even us?
- [ZIPPER ZIPS CLOSE]

250
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,367
- Huh?
- Maybe I'll give you some.

251
00:13:11,367 --> 00:13:12,700
- Just a little!
- Bastard.

252
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,167
- [BONG CLICKS TONGUE]
- [DOOR OPENS]

253
00:13:14,167 --> 00:13:16,367
- It's Gabo.
- He's here.

254
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:18,800
Gabo, what took you so long?

255
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,800
Where are the food and drinks?

256
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,067
I'm starving and we're parched!

257
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:29,133
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:13:29,133 --> 00:13:31,933
Sam, you don't have to...

259
00:13:31,933 --> 00:13:34,400
bottle your feelings up
all on your own.

260
00:13:34,733 --> 00:13:36,233
You can confide in me.

261
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:38,300
I'll listen. Really.

262
00:13:39,067 --> 00:13:40,833
With everything that's happened,

263
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:43,300
I got suspended.

264
00:13:43,733 --> 00:13:45,933
- The team got involved.
- Hmm.

265
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:49,267
Karen got hurt too.

266
00:13:49,267 --> 00:13:52,433
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:13:52,433 --> 00:13:55,533
I have no idea
how to deal with this.

268
00:13:57,267 --> 00:13:59,567
I don't know how I'm going
to tell my daddy about this.

269
00:13:59,967 --> 00:14:00,967
[SCOFFS]

270
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:04,433
The daughter of an NLEA Chief...

271
00:14:04,867 --> 00:14:06,333
is a failure.

272
00:14:07,467 --> 00:14:09,667
My daddy was probably right.

273
00:14:09,867 --> 00:14:10,867
I'm no good.

274
00:14:10,867 --> 00:14:12,667
Sam, Sam, Sam.

275
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:14,967
That mission...

276
00:14:15,567 --> 00:14:18,767
doesn't define who you are.

277
00:14:18,767 --> 00:14:24,700
One more thing, you just did
what you thought was right

278
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,700
based on the situation at hand.

279
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:29,600
Problem is, you just violated
our protocols.

280
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:32,300
But that doesn't mean
that what you did was wrong.

281
00:14:33,633 --> 00:14:35,333
That's where the problem lies.

282
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:36,833
How can I be a public servant

283
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:40,333
if I can't even abide
by the law myself?

284
00:14:40,333 --> 00:14:42,033
No. Look, Sam.

285
00:14:42,533 --> 00:14:43,433
Sam.

286
00:14:45,067 --> 00:14:46,333
You're a leader.

287
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:47,833
Okay?

288
00:14:48,233 --> 00:14:50,500
You're not a follower.

289
00:14:51,733 --> 00:14:53,133
And sometimes,

290
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:55,100
you have to cross that line

291
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:58,633
to be the leader that you are.

292
00:14:58,633 --> 00:15:00,233
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,633
- Hmm?
- [PATTING]

294
00:15:02,267 --> 00:15:03,567
[PATS]

295
00:15:03,567 --> 00:15:05,367
Hmm. Thanks.

296
00:15:05,367 --> 00:15:06,433
Mm-hmm.

297
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:08,000
[BOTTLES CLINK]

298
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:13,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:15:13,267 --> 00:15:14,900
- [BINOY]<i> It can!
</i>- [TOLITS] Yeah, it can--

300
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,467
- Shh!
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:15:16,467 --> 00:15:18,667
[CLEARS THROAT] There's puke
all over the place!

302
00:15:20,867 --> 00:15:22,667
[DOOR CREAKS CLOSE]

303
00:15:22,867 --> 00:15:24,033
[ZIPPER ZIPS OPEN]

304
00:15:24,767 --> 00:15:25,900
[ZIPPER ZIPS OPEN]

305
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:32,833
[PEE SPLASHING]

306
00:15:32,833 --> 00:15:39,800
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:15:40,833 --> 00:15:42,500
What are you looking at, huh?

308
00:15:43,133 --> 00:15:44,200
Nothing.

309
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:46,833
What do you mean, nothing?

310
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:48,133
You were taking a peek.

311
00:15:48,933 --> 00:15:50,000
What?

312
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:51,633
Am I your type?

313
00:15:52,233 --> 00:15:53,300
No.

314
00:15:53,867 --> 00:15:55,100
[BINOY] What's wrong, Daboy?

315
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,433
[TOLITS] Is there a problem?

316
00:15:57,433 --> 00:15:58,500
Wait a minute.

317
00:15:59,233 --> 00:16:00,467
I know you guys.

318
00:16:01,133 --> 00:16:04,033
You're those three bastards
who ran into us in Chinatown.

319
00:16:04,033 --> 00:16:06,733
Hey, who're you calling
bastards? Us?

320
00:16:06,733 --> 00:16:08,767
And we didn't ran into you.

321
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:11,800
- You were blocking the way.
- Hey, Tolits, that's enough!

322
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,800
We're no match for them.
They're huge!

323
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,767
So what if they're huge?
You scared?

324
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:18,367
You think we're small?
You think he's small?

325
00:16:18,367 --> 00:16:19,967
Don't point at me.

326
00:16:19,967 --> 00:16:22,767
That's right? Wh-- why,
you wanna fight, huh?

327
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:24,500
Think you can get us?

328
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,167
You want to get a taste
of my fists?

329
00:16:26,167 --> 00:16:28,367
- You, wanna go at it?
- [BLOW LANDS]

330
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,100
[BINOY] What happened? Huh?

331
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:33,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:36,500
Oh, so you're pretending
that it doesn't hurt, huh?

333
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,900
- He's trying to look tough.
- For sure.

334
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,233
You're enduring it, huh?

335
00:16:39,233 --> 00:16:40,433
- Take this! [GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

336
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:43,300
[BINOY] Get him, Tolits!
Get his ass!

337
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:44,767
It's useless. [PANTING]

338
00:16:44,767 --> 00:16:47,233
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

339
00:16:47,233 --> 00:16:50,067
- [GRUNTING]
- Do it faster! Harder!

340
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:52,067
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [WHIMPERS]

341
00:16:52,067 --> 00:16:54,033
Ow, it hurts! I'm the one
who's getting hurt.

342
00:16:54,033 --> 00:16:55,567
It hurts. [INHALES SHARPLY] Ow!

343
00:16:55,567 --> 00:16:58,333
[CHANTING] I don't want
to fight, I don't want to fight.

344
00:16:58,833 --> 00:17:00,733
- Is that it?
- What do you mean, is that it?

345
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:03,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS IN PAIN] Ow!

346
00:17:03,233 --> 00:17:10,167
- [BLOWS LANDING]
-[BINOY, TOLITS, DABOY GROANING]

347
00:17:10,167 --> 00:17:15,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:16,733
That hurts!

349
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,000
You know, Sam, [CLEARS THROAT]

350
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,267
I was thinking...

351
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:25,167
why don't we go on a vacation?

352
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:26,867
What do you think?

353
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:29,900
We could go to Boracay.

354
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:32,733
- Or even Europe or America.
- [LAUGHS]

355
00:17:32,733 --> 00:17:34,067
Maybe Australia.

356
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,767
Anywhere we could unwind.

357
00:17:36,967 --> 00:17:40,400
Away from our problems,
from all of this.

358
00:17:40,733 --> 00:17:43,767
- What do you say?
- No need. It's fine.

359
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,633
You sure?

360
00:17:46,633 --> 00:17:47,867
I am.

361
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:52,667
Uh... okay. But don't worry,
I'll take care of your case.

362
00:17:52,933 --> 00:17:55,167
Okay? I'll fix it.

363
00:17:55,167 --> 00:17:56,333
Don't worry.

364
00:17:56,567 --> 00:17:57,733
I got your back.

365
00:17:57,933 --> 00:17:59,233
Aren't you reliable?

366
00:17:59,233 --> 00:18:00,500
- Of course!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

367
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:03,333
Count on it.

368
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:10,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

369
00:18:10,033 --> 00:18:11,633
What did Delgado say?

370
00:18:16,167 --> 00:18:17,300
Was it about me?

371
00:18:17,967 --> 00:18:21,767
Sam, they're already building
up a case against you.

372
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:23,900
They also want to file
a petition

373
00:18:23,900 --> 00:18:26,267
against you to kick you out
of the agency.

374
00:18:26,267 --> 00:18:28,500
[SEBASTIAN CLICKS TONGUE]
It's just a petition.

375
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,200
It's not yet the final decision.

376
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:33,367
Know what, we can still
turn things around.

377
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,200
We can still correct it.

378
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,900
Sam, when the team did
a clean up

379
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,400
at the area of operation,

380
00:18:40,633 --> 00:18:42,667
they never found a case
containing gold bars in it.

381
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,500
- Where is it then?
- [RALLOS] Ma'am,

382
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:46,300
even if
it's an illegal operation,

383
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:50,233
maybe we could try to use it
as an evidence against Mr. Chan

384
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:51,900
if we find that gold.

385
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:54,100
We need to find the gold.

386
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:59,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:18:59,033 --> 00:19:01,333
Oh, by the way,
where'd those three go?

388
00:19:01,633 --> 00:19:03,833
To the bathroom. They still
haven't come back though.

389
00:19:03,833 --> 00:19:05,733
- [GRUNTS, PANTING]
- [DABOY] Have mercy, boss!

390
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:07,800
We'll sue you!

391
00:19:08,233 --> 00:19:10,800
We'll sue you with child abuse
and uh...

392
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:13,000
- libel!
- You're going to sue us

393
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,433
when you started it?!

394
00:19:15,833 --> 00:19:17,633
Look. We're NCIA agents!

395
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:18,867
What if we beat you up
for real?!

396
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,033
Please don't, sir!

397
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:21,433
Let's frisk them they might
have firearms on them!

398
00:19:21,433 --> 00:19:22,633
I have nothing, sir! Ow!

399
00:19:22,633 --> 00:19:24,333
I don't even have money
on me, sir!

400
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:26,033
We're broke as hell, sir!

401
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:27,767
I told you, it's empty!

402
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:30,167
- Nothing.
- I got nothing, sir!

403
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,600
Ack! Ow!

404
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:37,933
- [ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]
- [MUFFLED SCREAMS]

405
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:39,200
[DOOR OPENS]

406
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:41,500
- [SCREAMS]
- Hey, that's enough!

407
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,200
- What on earth happened?
- It's these bastards!

408
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,933
They're cocky
and messed with us!

409
00:19:45,933 --> 00:19:49,300
That's enough. Let's avoid
getting into trouble. Let's go!

410
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,800
That's enough. Let's just go.

411
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:53,333
You should be thankful
we still have somewhere to be.

412
00:19:53,333 --> 00:19:55,100
[TOLITS] Thank you!

413
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,233
It's your fault!

414
00:19:56,233 --> 00:19:59,100
You kept staring at him!
Was he your type, huh?!

415
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:01,267
[CASTOR] Hey, guys,
why did you do that?

416
00:20:02,033 --> 00:20:03,433
Come on, guys!

417
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:06,167
We're already going through
enough problems as it is.

418
00:20:06,167 --> 00:20:09,033
If those men filed a complaint
against us,

419
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,900
we might be suspended for real.

420
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:13,133
Sorry, Tony. It's my bad.

421
00:20:13,133 --> 00:20:14,100
[SIGHS]

422
00:20:14,567 --> 00:20:16,200
Fix yourselves up.

423
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:18,767
Hurry up. Ma'am Sam's
waiting for us.

424
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:23,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

425
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:26,567
Sir.

426
00:20:26,567 --> 00:20:29,033
Have you talked to Paquito?

427
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:31,333
Who was the man
they encountered?

428
00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:32,800
Sir, they don't know.

429
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,567
They weren't the ones
who fought him.

430
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,767
They just ordered their
incompetent men to do it.

431
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:40,100
They fought one guy,
but all of them got beaten.

432
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,200
They're useless!

433
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,167
What we pay them
is just a waste.

434
00:20:43,733 --> 00:20:45,033
[UMALI] Sir.

435
00:20:45,033 --> 00:20:46,767
That's why I didn't pay them.

436
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:48,567
Paquito apologized.

437
00:20:48,567 --> 00:20:51,900
But Django is just arrogant.

438
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:53,900
I nearly hit him earlier.

439
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:58,033
I want to know the identity
of the person they fought.

440
00:20:58,033 --> 00:20:59,833
Check whether
there is CCTV footage.

441
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:04,300
Find the man who
went up against Paquito's men.

442
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,800
We might find him useful.

443
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:10,867
Yes, sir.

444
00:21:12,133 --> 00:21:13,333
[SIGHS]

445
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:17,433
- Here's our food.
- [IPE] Finally!

446
00:21:17,433 --> 00:21:18,500
[TEKLA] You guys
are too impatient.

447
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,467
[IPE] It took so long.

448
00:21:19,467 --> 00:21:20,967
[TEKLA] Wow!

449
00:21:20,967 --> 00:21:22,767
Where are the three scumbags?

450
00:21:22,767 --> 00:21:24,400
They're the ones who
are always in a rush to eat.

451
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,667
- Call them!
- Where are they?

452
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,300
- Let's call them.
- Let's go.

453
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:28,467
They're taking too long.

454
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:29,700
[TEKLA] I wonder
what they're doing?

455
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:31,100
[UTENSILS CLATTERING]

456
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,433
Your beer's warm.

457
00:21:36,467 --> 00:21:38,133
- [SIGHS]
- Where did you go?

458
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,567
[CASTOR] To the bathroom.

459
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,100
[TEKLA] Are you okay, Gabo?

460
00:21:42,133 --> 00:21:43,367
What's going on?

461
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:45,767
I saw something.

462
00:21:47,133 --> 00:21:48,367
I saw something I didn't like.

463
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:50,433
You saw something?
What is it?

464
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,667
[BOTTLE CLATTERS]

465
00:21:54,633 --> 00:21:55,700
Forget it.

466
00:21:56,433 --> 00:21:59,533
We should've had drinks
at Linda's store instead.

467
00:21:59,533 --> 00:22:00,833
There are no bad vibes there.

468
00:22:00,833 --> 00:22:02,500
The service here
takes too long.

469
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,800
If that's the case,

470
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:09,433
then I'll go ahead and eat.
I'm starving.

471
00:22:09,433 --> 00:22:16,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

472
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,433
- [GROANS]
- Hey!

473
00:22:19,433 --> 00:22:20,667
- What happened?
- Hey!

474
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:23,867
We were attacked.
Didn't you see them?

475
00:22:23,867 --> 00:22:25,733
Let's go!
We might catch up to them!

476
00:22:25,733 --> 00:22:27,467
Help me! I can't stand!

477
00:22:27,467 --> 00:22:29,433
- [BONG] Let's go!
- [IPE] C'mon.

478
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,267
I'm heading out.

479
00:22:35,267 --> 00:22:36,900
I'm a bit tipsy.

480
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:38,167
- [KAREN] I'll go with you.
- [SEBASTIAN] Let's go.

481
00:22:38,167 --> 00:22:40,700
[RALLOS] I've got it, sir.
I'll get the beers.

482
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,500
- Sure.
- [KAREN] Let's go.

483
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,067
- [DABOY] Hurry up!
- [TOLITS] Let's go!

484
00:22:45,067 --> 00:22:47,033
- [GROANS]
- He's huge!

485
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:49,533
[BINOY] The one
who beat us was huge!

486
00:22:49,567 --> 00:22:51,033
Stop saying nonsense!
That's why you got beat up.

487
00:22:51,033 --> 00:22:53,067
We can't tell Gabo.

488
00:22:53,067 --> 00:22:55,300
This might be your fault.
We can't drag him into this.

489
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:57,733
[TOLITS] What do you mean?
We got beaten up!

490
00:22:57,733 --> 00:23:00,500
- [GROANS]
- Hurry! Hurry!

491
00:23:00,867 --> 00:23:02,567
[TEKLA] You should eat
with me, Gabo.

492
00:23:02,567 --> 00:23:04,633
Let's not wait
for those idiots anymore.

493
00:23:05,667 --> 00:23:08,467
They won't be upset
since you'll pay.

494
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:12,567
- [SEBASTIAN] Rallos?
- [RALLOS] Yes, sir?

495
00:23:12,567 --> 00:23:15,567
Take my car.
I'll bring Sam home.

496
00:23:15,567 --> 00:23:16,500
[DABOY] Ouch!

497
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:18,300
[BINOY] They were just here!

498
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,767
That man was huge!

499
00:23:19,767 --> 00:23:21,900
- Where is he?
- He looked like a wrestler!

500
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,567
- There were three of them!
- Where are they?

501
00:23:24,567 --> 00:23:26,900
Miss, have you seen
a huge man?

502
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:29,200
- Is it him?
- Maybe he left!

503
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,733
We should tell Gabo!

504
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:33,733
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

505
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:36,667
[TOLITS] We
got beaten up, Gabo!

506
00:23:36,667 --> 00:23:37,433
[TEKLA] What?!

507
00:23:37,433 --> 00:23:39,133
We got beaten up by the NCIA.

508
00:23:39,133 --> 00:23:41,100
- [BINOY GROANS]
- The NCIA again?!

509
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:43,067
Maybe they're
in the parking lot! Let's go!

510
00:23:43,067 --> 00:23:45,967
[TOLITS] Let's get back at them!

511
00:23:45,967 --> 00:23:46,867
Let's go!

512
00:23:47,333 --> 00:23:48,800
Sam, where are your keys?

513
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:50,033
Wait!

514
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:56,967
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

515
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:58,933
[DOOR CLICKS]

516
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,767
- [DOOR SLAMS]
- They're the NCIA.

517
00:24:04,767 --> 00:24:06,067
[ENGINE REVS]

518
00:24:07,233 --> 00:24:08,900
I'm sure they have
guns with them.

519
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:10,400
How will we get back
at them, Gabo?

520
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:14,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

521
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:16,200
We'll get even next time.

522
00:24:18,367 --> 00:24:20,033
That's the bastard
who beat me up.

523
00:24:24,100 --> 00:24:25,900
- [DOOR SLAMS]
- I'll get back at them.

524
00:24:26,933 --> 00:24:30,433
[CAR ENGINE REVS]

525
00:24:30,467 --> 00:24:35,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

526
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:37,533
[ENGINE REVS]

527
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,433
What's our plan, Gabo?

528
00:24:43,933 --> 00:24:45,167
We're leaving.

529
00:24:46,833 --> 00:24:47,600
Let's go.
Their service was bad anyway.

530
00:24:50,033 --> 00:24:51,767
[TEKLA] What a bummer!
We didn't even get to drink!

531
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:53,200
[BINOY]
Whose fault is it?

532
00:24:53,333 --> 00:24:55,700
- I wonder who!
- Why are you looking at us?!

533
00:24:55,833 --> 00:24:58,800
- Well, it is your fault.
- Gabo, join us!

534
00:24:58,933 --> 00:25:00,700
- Have a seat.
- Oh! Free booze!

535
00:25:00,833 --> 00:25:01,867
- Thank you!
- Simang!

536
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,000
Give these guys a bucket!
Put it on my tab.

537
00:25:04,167 --> 00:25:07,000
[BINOY] Is this spicy?
My wound still hurts.

538
00:25:07,133 --> 00:25:08,333
Hey, what happened to you?

539
00:25:08,467 --> 00:25:11,900
Well, Gabo here wanted to treat
us to some food and drinks.

540
00:25:12,033 --> 00:25:14,333
But since we were
with these three,

541
00:25:14,467 --> 00:25:15,933
we got in trouble.

542
00:25:16,067 --> 00:25:18,133
So, here we are,
parched and hungry.

543
00:25:18,933 --> 00:25:20,700
Who did you fight?

544
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:23,400
I heard they're from NCIA.

545
00:25:23,533 --> 00:25:25,000
That explains your faces.

546
00:25:25,133 --> 00:25:26,700
Simang, make sure
the beer's cold.

547
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,833
- Here you go.
- Pass it on.

548
00:25:42,267 --> 00:25:43,400
You're going out?

549
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,367
- It's already late.
- I'm going to work.

550
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:47,833
To work? Where?

551
00:25:47,967 --> 00:25:49,267
At The BeerGin Bar.

552
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:52,967
I told you Paquito allowed me
to work there, didn't I?

553
00:25:56,900 --> 00:25:58,433
- Betchay.
- Ow!

554
00:25:59,433 --> 00:26:01,533
You don't have to work
at The BeerGin.

555
00:26:01,667 --> 00:26:03,000
What was that?

556
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:05,900
Who's working at the BeerGin?

557
00:26:06,033 --> 00:26:08,567
Me. Do you have
a problem with that?

558
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:10,467
If you're worried about money,

559
00:26:10,633 --> 00:26:12,200
I can earn that
at the car repair shop!

560
00:26:12,333 --> 00:26:13,633
Just let me recover.

561
00:26:13,767 --> 00:26:15,267
If only I weren't injured,

562
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:17,000
you wouldn't have to worry
about a thing!

563
00:26:17,133 --> 00:26:18,333
That car repair shop?

564
00:26:18,467 --> 00:26:22,167
That car repair shop
that's always in the negative?

565
00:26:22,300 --> 00:26:25,600
Who gave you the capital
for that anyway?

566
00:26:27,133 --> 00:26:28,200
Hey!

567
00:26:28,333 --> 00:26:30,833
That's for everyone!
Don't eat it all!

568
00:26:30,967 --> 00:26:33,500
Sorry, but I'm really hungry.
We haven't had dinner yet.

569
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:36,767
Because we had to leave
before we could eat our order.

570
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:40,900
That's what you get
for always picking fights.

571
00:26:41,033 --> 00:26:46,267
You talk as if you're earning a
lot from that blasted bar!

572
00:26:46,433 --> 00:26:48,000
At least I'm doing something.

573
00:26:48,133 --> 00:26:51,100
I'm not sitting around
doing nothing.

574
00:26:51,233 --> 00:26:53,600
- There are other ways!
- What ways?

575
00:26:53,733 --> 00:26:55,533
Come on, tell me!

576
00:26:55,667 --> 00:26:59,267
<i>What can I possibly do
to quickly earn money</i>

577
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:02,967
enough to not worry about
all our expenses?!

578
00:27:03,100 --> 00:27:05,500
Do you know of a way?!
Tell me!

579
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:09,267
Can't think of anything,
can you?

580
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:12,533
<i> Unbelievable!</i>

581
00:27:12,667 --> 00:27:16,233
<i>I'm working hard here,
yet here you are judging me!</i>

582
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,500
[MAMENG] Why?

583
00:27:17,633 --> 00:27:20,733
Is The BeerGin the only place
you can work at?

584
00:27:20,867 --> 00:27:24,067
Have some respect
for your body!

585
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:26,267
- [SCOFFS]
- [DANTE] You know, Betchay,

586
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:28,233
our family's going to be
fodder for gossip

587
00:27:28,367 --> 00:27:29,967
when people find out
where you're working.

588
00:27:30,100 --> 00:27:31,967
I don't give a damn!

589
00:27:33,033 --> 00:27:34,167
That's Aunt Betchay.

590
00:27:34,300 --> 00:27:37,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

591
00:27:37,967 --> 00:27:39,867
Who's working
at Mister Paquito's bar?

592
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,533
Well, who do you think?

593
00:27:42,667 --> 00:27:46,333
It's your great stepmother,
Betchay.

594
00:27:46,467 --> 00:27:48,533
Of all the places
she could work at,

595
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:50,600
she just had to choose
Paquito's bar!

596
00:27:50,733 --> 00:27:52,967
Betchay, what were you thinking?

597
00:27:53,100 --> 00:27:56,733
Why'd you have to work
for Gabo's enemy?

598
00:27:56,867 --> 00:27:59,133
Aunt Betchay, what you're
doing is dangerous!

599
00:27:59,267 --> 00:28:01,400
What if Paquito and Django
get back at you?

600
00:28:01,533 --> 00:28:03,867
Paquito is a good businessman.

601
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,033
And I have nothing to do
with your fight with Django!

602
00:28:07,167 --> 00:28:10,433
You know what's the problem
with you lot?

603
00:28:10,567 --> 00:28:13,900
You keep thinking ill
of all my efforts!

604
00:28:14,033 --> 00:28:16,233
We're not demeaning
your efforts!

605
00:28:16,367 --> 00:28:19,867
All we're trying to say is
have some respect for body!

606
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,733
Have some respect
for yourself!

607
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:24,500
You want me to worry
about my body?

608
00:28:24,633 --> 00:28:26,600
We don't even have
enough to eat!

609
00:28:26,733 --> 00:28:28,733
What good is my pride, anyway?!

610
00:28:28,867 --> 00:28:32,400
I'm so sick of being poor!

611
00:28:32,533 --> 00:28:34,867
I just want a better life!

612
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:39,833
Now, I have the chance
to earn some cash,

613
00:28:39,967 --> 00:28:41,700
so I'll make the most of it!

614
00:28:41,833 --> 00:28:43,233
If that's what you want...

615
00:28:44,433 --> 00:28:46,033
then suit yourself!

616
00:28:46,167 --> 00:28:47,600
Oh, I will!

617
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,900
And you!

618
00:28:53,033 --> 00:28:54,467
You're the bane of my existence!

619
00:28:54,600 --> 00:29:01,467
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

620
00:29:06,533 --> 00:29:08,133
<i> I think they want to kill me</i>

621
00:29:08,267 --> 00:29:12,533
<i>because I spoke against
Ricardo Jacinto and the cops</i>

622
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:14,867
<i>who were out to demolish
Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

623
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,967
<i>Looks like that reporter
is out to get you.</i>

624
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:19,000
<i>Things aren't looking good
for that project.</i>

625
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:22,333
<i>I know it was Aunt Betchay
who hustled to provide for us.</i>

626
00:29:22,467 --> 00:29:26,433
<i>And I witnessed how hurt
you were when Mama died.</i>

627
00:29:26,567 --> 00:29:28,533
<i>But, Papa,
please don't lose hope.</i>

628
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,233
<i> I'm here to help you.</i>

629
00:29:30,367 --> 00:29:33,567
<i>I hope you find a woman
who will truly love you</i>

630
00:29:33,700 --> 00:29:35,733
<i> and help you change your life.</i>

631
00:29:35,867 --> 00:29:39,333
<i>If I find a woman to love,
I'll try to be like you.</i>

632
00:29:39,467 --> 00:29:42,067
<i>Because I saw how much
affection you had for Mama,</i>

633
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:43,967
<i> how you took care of her,</i>

634
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:46,033
<i>and how you
made us feel loved.</i>
